Mirrors the Department page's CMS wiring for the Secretariat page:

- New Sanity schemas: secretariatDetail, secretariatActivity,
  secretariatResourceGroup, secretariatResourceFile — same shape as
  their department* counterparts, keyed by `section` (sg, events,
  meetings, advocacy, sustainability, publications) instead of
  `department`. Registered in studio/schemas/index.ts and added to the
  Studio structure list.
- New src/app/data/sanitySecretariatResources.ts with hooks
  (useCmsSecretariatDetail, useCmsSecretariatActivities,
  useCmsSecretariatActivity, useCmsSecretariatResourceGroups,
  useCmsSecretariatResourceFiles) mirroring sanityDepartmentResources.ts.
- SecretariatResources.tsx now renders CMS detail content (hero,
  overview/key focus areas or full article, section-head card), an
  Activities & Milestones section, and CMS resource groups — falling
  back to the existing hardcoded copy exactly as DepartmentResources.tsx
  does, with the same loading skeleton to avoid a fallback-then-swap
  flash.
- New SecretariatActivityDetail.tsx (mirrors DepartmentActivityDetail.tsx)
  and route /secretariat/:sectionId/activities/:slug.
- SecretariatResourceFiles.tsx now prefers CMS-sourced files, falling
  back to the hardcoded file list.
- scripts/migrate-secretariat-detail-pages.mjs seeds the 6
  secretariatDetail documents from the same trilingual copy the
  Secretariat page itself already uses (secretariatPage.<key> in
  src/locales/*/home.json) — dry-run by default, --apply to write,
  create-only (never overwrites existing Studio content). Resource
  groups/files and activities are separate collections, added in Studio
  by staff, matching how department resources/activities are managed.

Verified: pnpm build clean, studio `sanity build` clean (no schema
errors), and end-to-end via Playwright against a mocked CMS response
(detail/head/overview/keyActivities, activities list + detail,
resource groups) plus the no-CMS-data fallback path — all render
correctly with no console errors.

